Example rules, in priority order (they show the syntax; they are not a good schedule for this system):
```
{"condition": "stage = CHECK & to_tails <= 0", "action": "p2"}
{"condition": "tails_decided & stage = WRITE & coin = TAILS", "action": "any"}
{"condition": "pc1 = FLIP & to_heads > 0", "action": "p1"}
{"condition": "!finished", "action": "any"}
```
Rule 1 lets process 2 check when that check would decide tails. Rule 2, once some process has decided tails, allows every process that is about to write a tails coin to move. Rule 3 lets process 1 flip while the counter is below the heads barrier. The last rule is a catch-all that allows every process that has not finished.
